  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Markets Asssesment for UMP and Gokwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main purpose of the market assessment is to investigate the impact of the ongoing economic challenges on the functionality of the markets and make recommendations on best modality of assistance by humanitarian actors. More specifically the market assessment will:
&#x2022;	Understand the supply chain of mainly cereals and other basic food commodities critical to food security of vulnerable households.
&#x2022;	Assess the market linkages between the surplus and the deficit districts within the country and establish possible market intervention points that can support access to food by the poor and vulnerable households during lean periods.
&#x2022;	Determine ability of the markets to respond to increased demand for cereals and other food commodities;
&#x2022;	Identify any potential risks associated with increased local demand arising from the use of cash transfers given the cash crisis being experienced in the two districts</narrative>
  </description>
